{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"wakeful-ordinary-chicken","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"# /var/gerrit data disk filled and has stayed near-full; review-bot went unhealthy\n\n## Impact (stated first)\nThe Gerrit/review-bot box (`i-00880b2c7f13527c5`, region us-east-1) suffered a box-wide\ndisk-fill starting **2026-08-26 ~15:00 PDT**. The `/var/gerrit` data disk jumped from a\n~55–59% baseline to **93–95% within ~6h and has NOT recovered** — it is still **94%** and the\nalarm `rebar-gerrit-data-disk-high` is **still in ALARM** at the time of this sweep\n(2026-08-29 10:00 PDT). During the fill, `rebar/host:reviewbot_healthy` **dropped to 0**\n(unhealthy) for two multi-hour windows, so LLM-Review capacity was degraded. Gerrit itself\nstayed up (`gerrit_healthy`=1, `Rebar/Gate:GerritReachable`=1 throughout).\n\n## Evidence — CloudWatch (namespace rebar/host, InstanceId i-00880b2c7f13527c5)\n\n### `rebar-gerrit-data-disk-high` alarm\n- `describe-alarm-history`: **OK -> ALARM at 2026-08-26T17:55:32 PDT**; no return-to-OK since.\n- StateReason: \"1 datapoint [88.0 (27/08/26 00:50Z)] >= threshold (85.0)\".\n\n### `disk_used_percent` mount=/var/gerrit (Maximum/hour, PDT)\n- Baseline: 52% (08-25 17:00) rising slowly to 59% (08-26 14:00).\n- **Sharp climb**: 08-26 15:00 = 64% -> 16:00 = 81% -> 17:00 = **88%** -> 18:00-20:00 = 89% ->\n  21:00 = **93%**.\n- **Plateau, unrecovered**: 93-95% continuously from 08-26 21:00 through 08-29 10:00\n  (latest datapoint **94%**). Trend: plateaued high, not draining.\n\n### `reviewbot_healthy` (Min/hour = 0 means unhealthy) — service impact\n- **0** for 08-26 15:00,16:00,17:00,18:00,20:00,21:00 PDT (coincides with the data-disk climb).\n- **0** again for 08-28 16:00-20:00 PDT (coincides with the root-disk thrash + deploy backpressure below).\n\n### Correlated root-disk pressure on the same box (30-GiB gp3 root, `root_disk_used_percent`)\n- `rebar-root-disk-pressure` **flapped into ALARM ~18 times** 08-26 20:41 -> 08-28 10:45 PDT.\n- Root usage oscillated 76-**98%** (peaks: 98% @08-26 15:00, 98% @08-28 01:00), then relaxed\n  to ~72-82% after 08-28 11:00.\n- `disk_pressure_prunes` ran **continuously ~5-6/hour for ~24h** (08-27 10:00 -> 08-28 10:00 PDT)\n  — the automated reclaim was working overtime and the root disk still sat near-full, matching\n  the \"reclaim frees nothing\" symptom of the closed root-disk tickets.\n\n### Downstream backpressure (08-28 16:00-20:00 PDT, review-bot unhealthy again)\n- `deploy_errors`: Sum=1 at 08-28 16:00 and 17:00 PDT -> `rebar-autodeploy-errors` ALARM\n  17:07->17:47 PDT.\n- `review_interrupts_bound_exceeded`: 08-28 16:00, 18:00, 19:00 (alarm flapped 3x);\n  `review_interrupts_signal_unavailable`: 08-28 17:00 (alarm 17:07->17:22).\n- `deploy_deferrals` climbed to Max 19-20/period on 08-28 evening — autodeploy repeatedly\n  deferred, consistent with disk pressure + in-flight reviews.\n  (Caveat: some marker-delta counters can over-report on a cold-start republish per closed\n  bug e2a6 widespread-zealous-narwhal; but the co-timed `reviewbot_healthy`=0 and root-disk\n  peaks make a real backpressure episode the stronger reading.)\n\n## Likely common cause (hypothesis)\nA large repository/pack growth landed on the box around 08-26 15:00 PDT, filling both\n`/var/gerrit` and root simultaneously. This is corroborated by CI's repo-growth guard tripping\nthe same day: `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml` step **\"Fail closed if the blobless\ncheckout pack exceeds its limit\"** (`REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB`, git `size-pack`), plus the\nmirror pack-size limits. Candidate on-disk consumers to confirm on the box: git repo/pack\ngrowth under `/var/gerrit` (tickets-branch and mirrors), Gerrit review artifacts/caches,\ndocker layers/build cache, and journald/logs.\n\n## What this ticket is NOT (dedup)\n- No existing ticket covers the **`/var/gerrit` data disk** mount; all prior disk tickets are\n  the **root** volume or docker cache (3a52 masonic-abeyant-stagbeetle, 9bc0\n  taurine-smiling-hamadryad, 7a41 forgivable-nerdy-genet — all closed). The data-disk high +\n  sustained-non-recovery is a distinct, currently-active condition.\n- The 08-28 root-disk flapping recurs the closed root-disk-pressure symptom (3a52); linked\n  relates_to for context rather than as this ticket's headline.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Identify what consumed `/var/gerrit` on 08-26 (du breakdown on the box: git/packs vs\n      review artifacts vs docker vs logs) and confirm/deny the pack-growth hypothesis.\n- [ ] Reclaim or grow `/var/gerrit` so `disk_used_percent` returns below the 85% threshold and\n      `rebar-gerrit-data-disk-high` clears (operator action — READ-ONLY sweep did not remediate).\n- [ ] Confirm `reviewbot_healthy` returns to steady 1 and stays there.\n- [ ] Add a guard/headroom or growth alarm so a repeat pack-growth event does not silently sit\n      at 93-95% for days (portable: not tied to a single CI provider).\n\n## Constraints / notes\n- Filed by a READ-ONLY AWS ops sweep (window 2026-08-26T17:55 PDT -> 2026-08-29T10:00 PDT). No\n  AWS mutation performed. Remediation (disk cleanup / volume resize) is an operator action.\n- Box logs are NOT shipped to CloudWatch Logs in us-east-1 (only lmn-*/snap-* groups exist), so\n  on-box `du`/journald inspection is required to finish root-cause — see sweep blind-spot note.\n","id":"5a05-0e52-33a0-48bf","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["ops","aws-sweep","disk-pressure","gerrit-box","review-bot"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"[gerrit-data-disk-high] /var/gerrit sustained ≥93% since 2026-08-26 (still ALARM at 94%); box-wide disk-fill drove review-bot unhealthy"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788023687551129237,"uuid":"9c0be22a-f1ef-4331-b3ec-28b0798496fc"}